# Food Swipe -- Supabase environment configuration
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com/dashboard (free tier is fine).
#   2. In your project: Project Settings -> API, copy the "Project URL" and
#      the "anon public" API key into the two values below.
#   3. Apply the SQL migrations in supabase/migrations/ to your project,
#      either by pasting each file's contents into the Supabase Dashboard's
#      SQL Editor and running them in order (0001, then 0002), or, if you
#      have the Supabase CLI installed and linked to this project, by
#      running `supabase db push` from the project root.
#   4. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values below. `.env` is
#      gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Astro only exposes environment variables prefixed with PUBLIC_ to
# client-side code (see https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/environment-variables/).
# The anon key is safe to expose to the browser -- it is designed for that --
# as long as Row Level Security policies (see supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql)
# are enabled on every table, which they are in this project.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# ===========================================================================
# Affiliate tracking for delivery links (Phase 5 -- monetization)
# ===========================================================================
#
# ALL OPTIONAL. The app works completely with none of these set, which is
# the state it ships in today: every delivery link is emitted as a plain
# public search URL, no disclosure is shown, and nothing is broken or
# missing. Setting one turns that service's links into tracked links; the
# affiliate disclosure then appears in the UI automatically, because the
# app only ever discloses a commercial relationship it actually has.
#
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. These are deliberately NOT PUBLIC_-prefixed, so Astro
# never ships them to the browser. Never commit real values -- `.env` is
# gitignored, this file is the template. On a host (Vercel etc.) set them as
# project environment variables; locally they must be in the *process*
# environment, which is what `.env` + `astro dev` and
# `node --env-file=.env ...` both give you.
#
# Each service takes up to three variables:
#
#   AFFILIATE_<SERVICE>_TEMPLATE
#       The tracking / redirect URL your affiliate network gives you, with
#       {url} where the destination goes. {id} is substituted from the _ID
#       variable below if present. The destination is URL-encoded for you.
#       This is how nearly every network works (Impact, Awin, CJ, Cuelinks
#       and friends all attribute via their own redirect domain).
#       Example shape only -- copy YOUR exact template out of your network's
#       dashboard, do not retype this one:
#           https://example-network.com/c/{id}/1234/5678?u={url}
#       Must be https and must contain {url}, or it is ignored and the plain
#       link is used.
#
#   AFFILIATE_<SERVICE>_ID
#       Your publisher / affiliate id. On its own it does nothing (an id
#       with no format to put it in attributes nothing) -- pair it with
#       _TEMPLATE, or with _PARAM below.
#
#   AFFILIATE_<SERVICE>_PARAM
#       Rare: for programs that attribute by a query parameter appended to
#       the destination itself rather than by a redirect. Set it to the
#       parameter name your program documents (and set _ID to the value).
#
# Where to sign up (networks change -- confirm the current one when you
# apply; the link format always comes from the network, never from us):
#
#   DOORDASH    US/CA/AU. Program runs through impact.com.
#               https://www.doordash.com/affiliates/
#   UBER_EATS   Most markets. impact.com or Partnerize, varies by country.
#   GRUBHUB     US. impact.com / CJ Affiliate.
#   ZOMATO      India. Via Indian aggregator networks -- Cuelinks, Admitad,
#               INRDeals. https://www.cuelinks.com/
#   SWIGGY      India. Same networks as Zomato.
#   DELIVEROO   UK/IE/FR/IT. Awin. https://www.awin.com/
#   JUST_EAT    UK/IE. Awin.
#   WOLT        Nordics/Baltics/EU. Country-level programs; commonly Awin or
#               a direct partnership.
#   LIEFERANDO  Germany (Just Eat Takeaway). Awin / Tradedoubler.
#
# Uncomment and fill in only the services you have actually been approved
# for. A service left blank keeps working as a plain link.

# AFFILIATE_DOORDASH_ID=
# AFFILIATE_DOORDASH_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_UBER_EATS_ID=
# AFFILIATE_UBER_EATS_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_GRUBHUB_ID=
# AFFILIATE_GRUBHUB_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_ZOMATO_ID=
# AFFILIATE_ZOMATO_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_SWIGGY_ID=
# AFFILIATE_SWIGGY_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_DELIVEROO_ID=
# AFFILIATE_DELIVEROO_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_JUST_EAT_ID=
# AFFILIATE_JUST_EAT_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_WOLT_ID=
# AFFILIATE_WOLT_TEMPLATE=
# AFFILIATE_LIEFERANDO_ID=
# AFFILIATE_LIEFERANDO_TEMPLATE=
